>
  <article class="article">
    <p class="eyebrow">Importer guide</p>
    <h1>Custom Tape Measures: What Importers Need to Know Before Ordering</h1>
    <p>Custom tape measures can support retail, promotional, distributor, and private-label programs. Before requesting a quote, buyers should prepare the details that affect cost, samples, production, and delivery.</p>
    <img src="/images/products/tape-measure-components/tape-measure-width-options.png" alt="Custom tape measure blade width options for private-label sourcing" width="1000" height="1000" />
    <h2>Product specifications</h2>
    <p>Confirm tape length, shell size, tape blade material, lock style, hook style, and whether the product needs a belt clip or wrist strap. These details help the supplier recommend a realistic model.</p>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Specification item</th><th>What to confirm</th><th>Why it matters</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Blade length</td><td>3m, 5m, 7.5m, 8m, 10m, 16ft, 25ft</td><td>Different markets expect different common sizes.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Blade units</td><td>Metric, inch, or dual-unit markings</td><td>Wrong unit choice can block sales in the target market.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Hook and strap</td><td>Standard hook, reinforced hook, magnetic hook, wrist strap</td><td>Small components affect user experience and complaints.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Packaging</td><td>Blister card, color box, display box, barcode, carton mark</td><td>Packaging affects retail readiness and warehouse receiving.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <h2>Branding options</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Logo on the case or label area</li>
      <li>Custom shell color</li>
      <li>Printed tape blade details</li>
      <li>Retail packaging artwork</li>
      <li>Barcode, carton mark, and private-label information</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>MOQ and lead time</h2>
    <p>MOQ may change based on color, printing, packaging, and production complexity. Lead time also depends on sample approval, packaging artwork approval, and order volume.</p>
    <h2>How to send a better RFQ</h2>
    <p>Include quantity, market, logo file, packaging preference, target price, delivery date, and any reference product photos. A detailed RFQ helps the supplier respond faster and more accurately.</p>
    <p>For a full product view, compare the <a href="/tape-measures/">tape measure manufacturer</a> category, the <a href="/custom-tape-measure/">custom tape measure supplier</a> options, the <a href="/products/custom-logo-tape-measure/">custom logo tape measure</a> page, and the <a href="/products/25ft-steel-tape-measure/">25ft tape measure supplier</a> page. Buyers planning a private label tape measure program should also review <a href="/quality-control/">tape measure quality control</a> before confirming bulk production.</p>
  </article>
